WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:33.125
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna taught us</b>

2
00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:39.791
<b>that one who gains control and peace of mind </b>
<b>becomes free from sorrows,</b>

3
00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:44.666
<b>and such a joyful person attains steady wisdom.</b>

4
00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:45.916
<b>Now,</b>

5
00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:51.041
<b> Krishna explains the </b>
<b>completely opposite situation.</b>

6
00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:56.125
<b>He describes the consequences </b>
<b>of letting the mind run unchecked.</b>

7
00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:05.000
<b>Lord Krishna says that a person </b>
<b>whose mind remains uncontrolled</b>

8
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.458
<b>has uncertain and unstable wisdom.</b>

9
00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:15.166
<b>Such a person can neither concentrate </b>
<b>on anything nor attain peace,</b>

10
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:19.583
<b>and how can one who is </b>
<b>restless ever find happiness?</b>

11
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:21.458
<b>The mind is extremely restless</b>

12
00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:28.541
<b>if left unchecked, it will run in all directions,</b>
<b>today here, tomorrow there,</b>

13
00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:29.750
<b>today this desire,</b>

14
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.041
<b>tomorrow another.</b>

15
00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:33.375
<b>This is the very instability of wisdom,</b>

16
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:38.083
<b>where one cannot focus in any single direction.</b>

17
00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:42.458
<b>They cannot evaluate situations with clarity.</b>

18
00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:47.875
<b>Consequently, their decisions lack permanence, </b>
<b>constantly changing.</b>

19
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:52.041
<b>What seems right today begins </b>
<b>to feel wrong tomorrow.</b>

20
00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:55.708
<b>This adversely affects every sphere of life</b>

21
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:57.958
<b>creating confusion in personal life,</b>

22
00:01:57.958 --> 00:02:01.208
<b>uncertainty in professional life,</b>

23
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.208
<b>and social life?</b>

24
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:04.500
<b>Think about it</b>

25
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:10.541
<b>how can anyone trust a person </b>
<b>whose decisions are not steady?</b>

26
00:02:10.541 --> 00:02:15.708
<b>As a result, it inevitably impacts</b>
<b>social relationships as well.</b>

27
00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:20.208
<b>In such a state, neither peace </b>
<b>nor happiness is found.</b>

28
00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:25.041
<b>Then restlessness gives birth</b>
<b>to even more instability.</b>

29
00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>Sometimes this cycle might begin small,</b>

30
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.500
<b>but</b>

31
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.833
<b>if the mind isn't restrained,</b>

32
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:35.291
<b>this cycle deepens progressively,</b>

33
00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.875
<b>and situations can deteriorate from bad to worse.</b>

34
00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:42.666
<b>What's needed is mind control.</b>

35
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:45.875
<b>To focus attention in the right direction.</b>

36
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:50.958
<b>What's needed is an </b>
<b>inclination toward spirituality.</b>

37
00:02:55.916 --> 00:03:00.500
<b>"Ashantasya kutah sukham"</b>

38
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.625
<b>Without peace,</b>

39
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:06.458
<b> where can happiness exist?</b>

40
00:03:06.458 --> 00:03:11.666
<b>Humans make countless efforts </b>
<b>to experience happiness.</b>

41
00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:13.375
<b>Fine clothes,</b>

42
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:15.208
<b>new possessions, </b>

43
00:03:15.208 --> 00:03:17.041
<b>good restaurants,</b>

44
00:03:17.041 --> 00:03:19.166
<b>entertainment devices,</b>

45
00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:20.916
<b>tourism expenses </b>

46
00:03:20.916 --> 00:03:24.083
<b>this list is endless.</b>

47
00:03:24.083 --> 00:03:25.208
<b>And</b>

48
00:03:25.208 --> 00:03:28.750
<b>earning money for all these...</b>

49
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.875
<b>all done in pursuit of happiness,</b>

50
00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:32.958
<b>yet</b>

51
00:03:32.958 --> 00:03:36.083
<b>unhappiness persists.</b>

52
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:41.666
<b>Because in chasing these sensory experiences,</b>

53
00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:45.833
<b>one has forgotten the fundamental </b>
<b>requirement of happiness.</b>

54
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:49.291
<b>The basic requirement for happiness is</b>

55
00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:52.375
<b>peace.</b>

56
00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:54.500
<b>If the mind is peaceful,</b>

57
00:03:54.500 --> 00:04:00.000
<b>even simple things will bring you joy.</b>

58
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.541
<b>But if the mind is restless,</b>

59
00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:10.041
<b>even the world's wealthiest </b>
<b>person will remain unhappy.</b>

60
00:04:10.041 --> 00:04:13.708
<b>Many minds ponder this question</b>

61
00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:21.208
<b>if wealth isn't the path to happiness, </b>
<b>is poverty the way?</b>

62
00:04:21.208 --> 00:04:24.541
<b>And here lies humanity's error</b>

63
00:04:24.541 --> 00:04:29.416
<b>seeking answers externally,</b>

64
00:04:29.416 --> 00:04:34.916
<b>comparing everything against </b>
<b>wealth and prosperity.</b>

65
00:04:34.916 --> 00:04:43.541
<b>Neither excess wealth nor its absence </b>
<b>has any connection to happiness.</b>

66
00:04:43.541 --> 00:04:48.458
<b>Happiness is connected only to the mind.</b>

67
00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:52.166
<b>To mental peace.</b>

68
00:04:52.166 --> 00:04:57.083
<b>This happiness lies within you, </b>
<b>this peace dwells inside you,</b>

69
00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:02.041
<b>merely invisible due to darkness.</b>

70
00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:07.666
<b>Light the lamp of spirituality, </b>
<b>illuminate your mind.</b>

71
00:05:07.666 --> 00:05:12.458
<b>There you'll find both peace and happiness.</b>

72
00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:24.125
<b>Sometimes, small tensions arise between </b>
<b>couples in a family.</b>

73
00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:27.916
<b>The cause could be anything</b>

74
00:05:27.916 --> 00:05:30.333
<b>disagreement on some matter,</b>

75
00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:31.833
<b>financial concerns,</b>

76
00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:35.833
<b>differences regarding children, and so forth.</b>

77
00:05:35.833 --> 00:05:38.500
<b>To escape such situations,</b>

78
00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:41.000
<b>to distract themselves,</b>

79
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.833
<b>people often seek refuge in other activities</b>

80
00:05:45.833 --> 00:05:48.291
<b>meeting a friend,</b>

81
00:05:48.291 --> 00:05:50.750
<b>getting busy with work,</b>

82
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:53.875
<b>watching a favorite show... and so on.</b>

83
00:05:53.875 --> 00:06:00.208
<b>These remedies are suitable</b>
<b>for temporary peace of mind,</b>

84
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:02.000
<b>But</b>

85
00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.916
<b>the problem escalates</b>

86
00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:10.125
<b>when running from situations becomes a habit,</b>

87
00:06:10.125 --> 00:06:14.958
<b>when ignoring mutual tension </b>
<b>seems appropriate.</b>

88
00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:19.916
<b>An ego fills the mind.</b>

89
00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:28.375
<b>Both parties constantly expect their partner </b>
<b>to come forward, apologize, initiate conversation.</b>

90
00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:35.375
<b>In such cases, though the house might </b>
<b>appear peaceful from outside,</b>

91
00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:39.000
<b>the mind remains constantly disturbed,</b>

92
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.291
<b>and joy vanishes from life.</b>

93
00:06:43.291 --> 00:06:48.875
<b>Ignoring mutual tension isn't right.</b>

94
00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:52.916
<b>Whether a crack appears in a wall</b>
<b>or in relationships,</b>

95
00:06:52.916 --> 00:06:56.291
<b>it's better to fill it quickly,</b>

96
00:06:56.291 --> 00:06:57.833
<b>otherwise,</b>

97
00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:03.541
<b>with time, that crack will only widen.</b>

98
00:07:03.541 --> 00:07:06.416
<b>Don't ignore mutual tensions</b>

99
00:07:06.416 --> 00:07:09.041
<b>what shame is there in apologizing,</b>

100
00:07:09.041 --> 00:07:12.500
<b>what ego in sitting down to talk?</b>

101
00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:17.458
<b>Who took the first step hardly matters.</b>

102
00:07:17.458 --> 00:07:19.958
<b>Husband and wife</b>

103
00:07:19.958 --> 00:07:26.083
<b>are both the foundation of the family. </b>
<b>They are one.</b>

104
00:07:26.083 --> 00:07:28.208
<b>No problem exists that</b>

105
00:07:28.208 --> 00:07:33.208
<b>can't be resolved through mutual </b>
<b>love and understanding.</b>

106
00:07:33.208 --> 00:07:36.125
<b>This is the path to family peace,</b>

107
00:07:36.125 --> 00:07:38.333
<b>and where there is peace,</b>

108
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:42.375
<b>there alone is happiness.</b>

109
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.791
<b>In professional life,</b>

110
00:07:48.791 --> 00:07:54.708
<b>decision-making ability is crucial for efficiency.</b>

111
00:07:54.708 --> 00:07:59.458
<b>Deciding right from wrong, choosing priorities,</b>

112
00:07:59.458 --> 00:08:02.208
<b>determining work methodology.</b>

113
00:08:02.208 --> 00:08:03.500
<b>However,</b>

114
00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.125
<b>if wisdom remains unstable,</b>

115
00:08:06.125 --> 00:08:13.625
<b>one cannot concentrate, </b>
<b>cannot properly assess situations,</b>

116
00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:15.875
<b>cannot make appropriate decisions.</b>

117
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:19.333
<b>This affects work efficiency.</b>

118
00:08:19.333 --> 00:08:23.375
<b>For an organization's success, it's essential</b>

119
00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:27.791
<b>that its people's decision-making improves.</b>

120
00:08:27.791 --> 00:08:33.875
<b>And for this, their concentration must strengthen.</b>

121
00:08:33.875 --> 00:08:36.708
<b>If the organization's collective goal</b>

122
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:39.791
<b>becomes everyone's personal goal,</b>

123
00:08:39.791 --> 00:08:43.375
<b>all will focus there,</b>

124
00:08:43.375 --> 00:08:46.375
<b>and every decision made with such focus</b>

125
00:08:46.375 --> 00:08:50.083
<b>will then be solely for the organization's success.</b>

126
00:08:50.083 --> 00:08:51.583
<b>But</b>

127
00:08:51.583 --> 00:08:54.625
<b>how to achieve this concentration,</b>

128
00:08:54.625 --> 00:08:57.458
<b>how to improve decision-making</b>

129
00:08:57.458 --> 00:09:00.625
<b>there are some methods:</b>

130
00:09:00.625 --> 00:09:01.916
<b>First</b>

131
00:09:01.916 --> 00:09:03.916
<b>Training</b>

132
00:09:03.916 --> 00:09:09.000
<b>by forming groups of experienced </b>
<b>and inexperienced people.</b>

133
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.666
<b>Here, seniors' experience will improve others' </b>
<b>decision-making.</b>

134
00:09:14.666 --> 00:09:15.750
<b>Second</b>

135
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.083
<b>Purpose Reminder</b>

136
00:09:18.083 --> 00:09:23.750
<b>it's essential to constantly repeat </b>
<b>the organization's purpose.</b>

137
00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:32.250
<b>How any significant change connects to</b>
<b>this purpose should be shared with all.</b>

138
00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:38.500
<b>This reinforces purpose awareness, </b>
<b>enhances decision-making.</b>

139
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:44.500
<b>Making collective progress the </b>
<b>measure of individual progress</b>

140
00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.541
<b> In everyone's annual assessment.</b>

141
00:09:46.541 --> 00:09:52.541
<b>include the organization's collective success </b>
<b>as a significant criterion.</b>

142
00:09:52.541 --> 00:09:57.583
<b>When collective success becomes </b>
<b>the basis for individual evaluation,</b>

143
00:09:57.583 --> 00:10:02.375
<b>naturally everyone will focus there.</b>

144
00:10:02.375 --> 00:10:05.125
<b>Concentration leads to clarity.</b>

145
00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:07.416
<b>Clarity leads to right decisions.</b>

146
00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:10.500
<b>And right decisions lead to success.</b>

147
00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.583
<b>Remember this equation of professional life.</b>

